      "body": "🚨 **BLOCKING: committed transient agent runtime state — revert before merge**\n\nThis hunk replaces the tracked `running.json` (`[]`) with a live snapshot of the dev agent's persistent-shell job table: shell command history, PIDs, timestamps, and a heredoc dumping source under development. It is machine-local runtime state, not code:\n\n- **Scope violation** — the ticket demands a pure, byte-identical refactor of five functions; nothing in gh-1009 warrants touching `.fah/` state. This file changes on every agent run, so committing it also guarantees perpetual merge churn.\n- **Info hygiene** — the blob embeds the dev session's full command log (paths, debugging of CI internals, probing commands). No credential is visible in *this* snapshot, but the same file can capture env dumps or tokens in another session — it must not ride PRs into main.\n\n`.fah/` is already in `.gitignore` (line 36); the file is only tracked because it was force-added historically. Fix for this PR:\n\n```bash\ngit checkout origin/main -- .fah/bash_jobs/running.json\ngit commit -m \"chore: drop transient .fah runtime state from the diff\"\n```\n\n(Un-tracking the whole `.fah/` directory is a separate housekeeping ticket — do not expand this PR's scope.)"
    }
  ],
